jobs.description:
Cigna\-Evernorth Services Inc. seeks a Software Engineering Senior Advisor for the Morris Plains, NJ location to provide counsel and advice to management on significant software engineering matters.


Responsibilities:

* Work on highly complex processes and projects, provide thought leadership and technical expertise across multiple disciplines, and complete complex software delivery assignments.
* Deliver solutions on the communication platform, as well as collaborate with technical product owners, business product owners, other engineering teams, solution architecture, vendors, infrastructure, CIP, release management, and other partners.
* Drive and promote software engineering best practices and ensure timely delivery of products and projects.
* Ensure that teams understand and deliver solutions that meet guidelines, as well as resolve issues.
* Involved in all phases of projects, from project inception, decomposition, design, solutioning, implementation, testing, deployment, and post implementation support. advise business partners regarding solutions, as well as contribute to the project planning process.
* Hybrid work schedule.

Qualifications:

* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Information Systems or related field and 5 years of experience.
* Must have experience with: Java;
* Spring;
* AWS;
* OpenShift;
* Linux;
* Windows;
* Oracle: MongoDB;
* Kafka;
* Unica;
* Splunk;
* Dynatrace;
* ServiceNow;
* Cursor;
* Microsoft Copilot;
* Jira; and
* Confluence.
* Hybrid work schedule.




If you will be working at home occasionally or permanently, the internet connection must be obtained through a cable broadband or fiber optic internet service provider with speeds of at least 10Mbps download/5Mbps upload.
For this position, we anticipate offering an annual salary of 130,200 \- 217,000 USD / yearly, depending on relevant factors, including experience and geographic location.
This role is also anticipated to be eligible to participate in an annual bonus plan.



At The Cigna Group, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits, with a focus on supporting your whole health. Starting on day one of your employment, you’ll be offered several health\-related benefits including medical, vision, dental, and well\-being and behavioral health programs. We also offer 401(k), company paid life insurance, tuition reimbursement, a minimum of 18 days of paid time off per year, paid holidays, and leaves of absence. For more details on our employee benefits programs, click here.  











